    "lawSection": "Real Property",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7110A\n\nSPONSOR: THOMAS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the Town of Oyster Bay to grant Sai\nMandir USA a real property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRelates to authorizing Sai Mandir to receive retroactive real property\ntax exempt status.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Notwithstanding any other provision of law to the contrary,\nthe assessor of the Town of Oyster Bay is hereby authorized to accept\nfrom Nori Foundation d/b/a Sai Mandir USA, an application for exemption\nfrom real property taxes pursuant to section 420-a of the Real Property\nTax Law, with respect to 2019-2020 assessment roll for a portion\n2019-2020 school taxes and with respect to the 2019-2020 assessment roll\nfor a portion of the 2019 general taxes and all of the 2020 general\ntaxes for the parcel owned by such not-for-profit corporation which is\nlocated at 57-59 West Old Country Road, town of Oyster Bay, county of\nNassau, otherwise known as Nassau County parcel ID section 46 block 260,\nlot 105. If accepted, the application shall be reviewed as if it had\nbeen received on or before the taxable status date established for such\nrolls.\n\nIf satisfied that such organization would otherwise be entitled to such\nexemption if such organization had filed an application for exemption by\nthe appropriate taxable status date, the assessor, upon approval by the\nTown of Oyster Bay board, may grant exemption from taxation on such\nassessment rolls and make the appropriate corrections of the subject\nrolls.\n\nSection 2 states effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSai Mandir USA is a not-for-profit tax-exempt organization that serves\nthe needy in the fields of medical relief, education, and community\nservices since 1999. The organization was gifted property in the Town of\nOyster Bay, County of Nassau. The land is being. used for administrative\nand community service purposes.\n\nWhile the organization is qualified to apply for a tax exemption under\nsection 420 of the Real Property Tax Law, due to the timing of the\npurchase, they could not apply for an exemption for the 2019 tax year.\nAs a result of being unable to file the property tax exemption, Sai\nMandir USA was liable for school and property taxes despite their not-\nfor-profit status. This legislation would allow the assessor to accept\nand act on an application for these tax years, giving Sai Mandir USA the\ntax relief they seek.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone noted to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
